e tech  in the commercial real estate industry  in new york  city three of our favorite things are  python  data and machine learning up next  is introduction to probability by joseph  k  blitzstein and jessica huang having  noted that probability holds immense  importance in the field of data science  this book introduces you to concepts of  probability  by taking real life problems as the  examples  if you're already familiar with the  basics of probability  this book will benefit you to further  your knowledge of the basic  concepts if you are completely new to  probability  then you will have to spend a little  extra time on this book  talking about the authors joseph  blitstein is the professor of the  practice and statistics at harvard  university  he has taught a wide range of  undergraduate and graduate probability  and statistical courses at harvard he  is also a chess expert and serves as  faculty advisor to the hardware chess  club  next we have r for data science by  garrett grohlmund and hadley wickham  this is a perfect book which introduces  you to r  for data science it will teach you about  many aspects of our programming language  focusing on data wrangling data  exploration  and data modeling with r this book also  provides you with different r  tools for solving various data problems  easily  and quickly this book is divided into  various sections  each section tackles different aspects  of data science  along with some exercises that will help  you to further understand the concepts  better  talking about the authors garrett  grolman has earned a bachelor's degree  in psychology from harvard university  he has also earned his phd in statistics  from rice university in 2012.  he works for our studio as both an  educator  and advocate of data science with r  hadley wickham is a statistician from  new zealand who is currently  chief scientist at our studio and an  adjunct professor of statistics at the  university  of auckland stanford university and  rice university his major fields are  statistics  data science and our programming  language  let us now look at some of the best  advanced level data science books  python data science handbook by jake  windplus a classic handbook for data  science in python  this book will introduce you to various  tools in python  like ipython numpy jupiter  pandas etc this book serves as a  comprehensive desk reference  that can be used by both beginners and  also experienced professionals  if you are someone who is well  acquainted with the basics of python and  data science  this is the best book to take your data  science skills and notch up  talking about the author jake vandeplas  was formerly both the director of open  software  and the director of research in physical  sciences  for e-science institute he comes from a  background of machine learning and data  intensive  astronomy and astrophysics  he received his bs in physics and  phd in astronomy up next we have  practical data science with r by john  mount  and nina zumel this book lives up to its  name  it explains the basic principles and  jumps  right into the real use cases that you  will face while collecting  curating and analyzing data  it shows you how to apply the r  programming language  and useful statistical techniques to  everyday business situations  it has established itself as the best  statistics book  for data science if you are looking  forward to seeing  yourself as a top data scientist you  should consider making this book as your  best friend  talking about the authors john mount is  the author of several  r packages his interests include  data science statistics r programming  and theoretical computer science he is  the co-founder  and principal consultant at win vector  llc  a san francisco data science consultancy  nina zumel is also a principal  consultant  at win vector llc a data science  consulting and training firm her  interests include  data science statistics statistical  learning  